# Definition of Done

The audit is complete only when:

* the website has been classified;
* relevant existing skills have been identified;
* an appropriate pipeline has been selected;
* relevant specialist audits have been executed;
* findings have evidence;
* assumptions are labeled;
* overlapping findings have been reconciled;
* root causes have been identified;
* conversion path has been analyzed;
* priorities have been established;
* a concrete improved website composition has been proposed;
* measurement gaps have been identified;
* final coverage and consistency checks have been performed.

If some stage could not be performed, explicitly state:

`NOT VERIFIED`

and explain why.

Never report an incomplete audit as fully complete.

  
